      "verified": true,
      "verified_by": "a_cached_stab_scratch_must_fit_two_addresses",
      "fine_trace_step": 12,
      "description": "Root cause. In the `H5G_CACHED_STAB` arm, vulnerable code decodes two `H5F_SIZEOF_ADDR(f)`-byte cached addresses from the root-entry scratch pad without checking whether that much space remains. On the witnessed path `pp` enters the scratch area at image offset 148, `H5F_SIZEOF_ADDR(f) == 16`, and the block demands 32 bytes from the fixed `H5G_SIZEOF_SCRATCH == 16` extent."
    },
